# bix-43-q5 — CBD/cisplatin combination: DE + Reactome_2022 enrichment

## Headline
The combination signature (Cisplatin_IC50_CBD_IC50 vs Untreated) is an **anti-proliferative
DNA-damage / p53 response with cell-cycle and metabolic shutdown**: TP53 target genes are
coordinately induced (FDXR, BTG2, CDKN1A, ZMAT3, TP53INP1, AEN, PHLDA3, TNFRSF10C, FAS, BAX,
GDF15-type programme), while the mitotic G2/M + E2F/G1-S proliferation programme, the
HIF-target glycolytic programme (GPI, ALDOA/ALDOC, ENO1/2, PGK1, LDHA, PFKFB3/4, ANKRD37,
HILPDA, ANGPTL4, BNIP3, PLOD2, VEGFA) and SREBP-driven cholesterol biosynthesis
(HMGCR, HMGCS1, SQLE, INSIG1/2, LDLR, MVK, MVD, DHCR7, FASN, SCD) are coordinately repressed.
Aryl-hydrocarbon-receptor / xenobiotic metabolism is the other strongly induced programme
(CYP1A1 +5.0x, AHRR +5.6x, CYP1B1 +2.5x, TIPARP, NQO1, ALDH1A3), i.e. CBD-driven AhR signalling.

**Not computable as specified:** gseapy could not be installed and no Reactome_2022 (or any
other) gene-set library exists in this offline sandbox, so the Reactome term string itself was
NOT computed. Everything below marked SUBSTITUTE uses a hand-curated marker panel, with the
identical Enrichr-style statistic (one-sided hypergeometric, library-as-background, BH).

## 1 Inputs
* counts_raw_unfiltered.csv: 63,677 x 30, int64 raw counts, no NA, no duplicate/non-ENSG row IDs,
  27,954 all-zero rows; columns `<group>_<replicate>` = 1_1..10_3 (10 groups x 3).
* sample_layout.csv: 10 groups x 3 replicates; SampleID `g-r` maps to column `g_r`.
  1 Untreated | 2 Serum_starvation | 3 DMSO | 4 DMSO_Serum_starvation | 5 Cisplatin_IC50 |
  6 Cisplatin_IC50_Serum_starvation_16h | 7 CBD_IC50 | 8 CBD_IC50_Serum_starvation_16h |
  9 Cisplatin_IC50_CBD_IC50 | 10 Cisplatin_IC50_CBD_IC50_Serum_starvation_16h.
  CBD alone = 7; cisplatin alone = 5; CBD+cisplatin = 9 (10 = same combo + serum starvation);
  control = 1 (Untreated); vehicles = 3 DMSO / 4 DMSO_Serum_starvation / 2 Serum_starvation.
* ensg_to_gene_name.tsv: 86,369 unique ENSG, 0 dup keys / 0 NA symbols; covers 53,636/63,677
  count rows = 84.23%; 7,247 symbols are shared by >1 ENSG.

## 2 Engine (no R, no pydeseq2 available) — `deseq_engine.py`
DESeq2-equivalent NB2 pipeline: median-of-ratios size factors -> NB GLM (design ~ Group, all
30 samples, cell-means so the Fisher information is block-diagonal) -> gene-wise dispersion by
df-corrected method of moments (DESeq2 `geneEstimator="moment"`; the profile-MLE version was
biased low, median d/truth 0.59, and inflated the null to 14%) -> parametric trend a0 + a1/x
(x = baseMean rather than min normalised count, because unfiltered matrices have zeros that blow
the 1/x term to the clip ceiling; shape/role unchanged) -> shrinkage mean(gene-wise, trend) ->
Wald contrasts on the fixed-dispersion refit. baseMean = mean of normalised counts.
Pre-filter: >=5 counts in >=3 samples (22,089 genes); baseMean>10 genes = 16,513.

Validation (`out/summary.json -> validation_simulation`, 10 groups x 3 reps, 2,000 genes,
100 planted DE in group 9 vs 1): size-factor log-correlation 0.9998; null-contrast fraction
p<0.05 = 0.062/0.064/0.056 (target 0.05, mildly anti-conservative as expected at n=3);
power at raw p<0.05 = 0.907 (empirical FDR of the raw-p rule 0.567 -> the briefed raw-p rule is
permissive, as expected); padj rule power 0.814, FDR 0.122; median |log2FC| error 0.29;
Jaccard of the shrunken vs unshrunken NB GLM DE lists 0.757.
Label-permutation calibration on the real counts: frac p<0.05 = 0.024/0.079/0.023.

