## 4 SUBSTITUTE enrichment, PRIMARY contrast 9 vs 1, raw-p list (1,899 symbols;
background = 20,814 symbol-mapped testable genes; 15 hand-curated panels tested)
| panel (hand-curated, NOT Reactome) | size | overlap | expected | P | adjusted P | direction (baseMean>10 members) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Hypoxia / glycolysis (HIF-target) | 31 | 23 | 2.8 | 4.1e-18 | 6.2e-17 | 29 down / 2 up, median LFC -0.77 |
| p53 / DNA-damage (TP53 targets) | 37 | 18 | 3.4 | 5.8e-10 | 4.3e-09 | 30 up / 6 down, median LFC +0.45 |
| AhR / xenobiotic metabolism | 13 | 8 | 1.2 | 4.0e-06 | 2.0e-05 | 10 up / 2 down, median LFC +0.69 |
| Circadian clock | 11 | 7 | 1.0 | 1.2e-05 | 4.6e-05 | mixed |
| EMT / adhesion / TGF-beta | 24 | 8 | 2.2 | 9.2e-04 | 2.7e-03 | mixed |
| ATF4 / integrated stress response | 18 | 6 | 1.6 | 4.1e-03 | 1.0e-02 | mixed |
Rank-based (Mann-Whitney on p-values, all genes) adds mitotic G2/M (1.3e-10, 29/29 down),
E2F/G1-S (2.9e-05), cholesterol/SREBP (1.1e-05, 25/26 down) and ribosome/translation (3.7e-06)
as coordinately shifted even though most members fall under |LFC|>0.5.

Control-invariance: the same two top panels (glycolysis down, p53 up) hold for 9 vs 1 and 9 vs 3
under both thresholds; in the serum-starved format (10 vs 4, 10 vs 2) the top panels are mitotic
G2/M down (28/29, q=2.4e-25) and cholesterol/SREBP down (q=1.2e-15) — i.e. the proliferative-arrest
component becomes dominant once the starved vehicle is the control. The anti-proliferative
DNA-damage/p53 + cell-cycle-down axis is present in all four contrasts.

Per-arm context (mean log2FC of panel vs Untreated): p53 targets cisplatin +0.62 / CBD -0.15 /
combo +0.59; AhR targets cisplatin +0.27 / CBD +0.95 / combo +0.99; mitotic genes cisplatin -0.04 /
CBD +0.09 / combo -0.42 (combo+SS -0.78). So the DNA-damage arm is cisplatin-driven, the AhR arm
CBD-driven, and the cell-cycle/metabolic shutdown is strongest with the combination.

Knowledge-free check: average-linkage clustering of the DE genes on group-mean log profiles
(r>=0.75) gives 161 modules; the largest (232 genes, median LFC -0.78) and second largest
(149 genes, -0.68) are dominated by the glycolysis/hypoxia/ATF4 genes, and the largest up-module
(125 genes, +0.71) contains THBS1, NR4A3, CCN1/CCN2, TFRC, TIPARP — independent of any panel.

## 5 To finish the requested analysis
`python3 run_enrichment_gseapy.py` (needs network + `pip install gseapy`) runs exactly
`gseapy.enrichr(gene_list=<1,899 symbols>, gene_sets="Reactome_2022", organism="human")` on the
pooled DE list plus up/down variants, writing `out/enrichment_gseapy_Reactome2022_*.csv`.
